    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s historic district covers 51 acres and includes 29 buildings that survived a 1898 fire.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imlaystown%2C_New_Jersey"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Salter's Mill, the town’s most recognizable landmark, sits on a 28‑acre millpond that once powered an ice business.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imlaystown%2C_New_Jersey"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ye Olde Yellow Meeting House, built in 1737, is one of the oldest surviving structures in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imlaystown%2C_New_Jersey"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Imlaystown’s post office operated from 1832 until its closure in 2009, marking over 170 years of service.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imlaystown%2C_New_Jersey"
    },
    {
